{
  "opening": "The marshmallow library is introducing new field types for IP interfaces and refining error handling within the Method field to ensure stricter validation and clearer error messages. The marshmallow-jsonschema consumer must update its dependency to accommodate these changes, specifically relying on the availability of the new interface fields and the corrected exception types during schema initialization.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m08",
      "text": "In the marshmallow library, the public names IPInterface, IPv4Interface, and IPv6Interface must be available as distinct field classes that serialize and deserialize valid IP network addresses according to their respective standards. Additionally, the public name IPv6 must remain accessible as a field class for serializing and deserializing IPv6 addresses."
    },
    {
      "id": "m16",
      "text": "In the marshmallow library, when using the public name Method, if a referenced schema method is missing, the system must raise an AttributeError rather than failing silently or raising a different exception type. Furthermore, errors related to invalid callables in the Method field must be raised at initialization time with appropriate type errors, ensuring that the public name set_value behaves consistently with strict callable validation."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure the marshmallow-jsonschema project pins its marshmallow dependency to version 0.13.0 or later to guarantee compatibility with these API updates."
}
